---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About — 10x Studio" description="A senior builder with cybersecurity and Fortune 500 software experience, an operator's eye for broken workflows, and a strategist's instinct for where software creates leverage." active="about">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero" style="background:var(--paper-2);">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="mk-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
          <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--blue">About</span>
          <span>One operator. Whole stack.</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="mk-h1">Senior partner.<br>Not a <span class="accent">department.</span></h1>
        <p>10x Studio is run by an engineer with cybersecurity and Fortune 500 software experience — and a long history of building the operational systems that make companies actually work. You'll talk to the person who would build it, not a sales engineer.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="/contact/" class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary mk-btn--lg">
            Start a Project Conversation <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/" class="mk-btn mk-btn--outline mk-btn--lg">See What We Build</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Brand color-block composition -->
      <div class="hero-art">
        <div class="cell" style="background:var(--ink-900); align-items:flex-end; justify-content:flex-start;">
          <span class="cell-label">Build</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cell" style="background:var(--blue-500);">
          <span class="circle" style="background:var(--yellow-500);"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cell" style="background:var(--yellow-500);">
          <span class="circle" style="background:var(--red-500);"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cell" style="background:var(--red-500); align-items:flex-end; justify-content:flex-end;">
          <span class="cell-label" style="text-align:right;">Operate</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BACKGROUND / WHAT I BRING -->
  <section class="mk-section">
    <div class="mk-wrap">
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr; gap:64px; align-items:start;" class="about-cols">
        <div>
          <div class="mk-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;"><b>//</b> Background</div>
          <h2 class="mk-h2" style="font-size:42px;">A builder's hands.<br>An operator's eye.</h2>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size:17px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--ink-700);">
          <p style="margin:0 0 18px;">Before 10x Studio, I spent years shipping enterprise software inside Fortune 500 environments and running cybersecurity programs where the cost of a sloppy build was measured in incident reports — not user complaints. That work shaped how I think about every system: the assumption is that real people will use it under real pressure, and the architecture has to survive that.</p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 18px;">I also spent years in operations and logistics leadership. That's where I learned that most software fails not because the code is wrong, but because the workflow underneath it was never properly understood. Spreadsheets become load-bearing infrastructure. Shared inboxes become unofficial CRMs. The right answer is rarely "buy another SaaS tool."</p>
          <p style="margin:0;">10x Studio is what happens when those backgrounds combine: a builder who treats your platform like it has to last, an operator who can see the broken process behind the feature request, and a strategist who can tell you when the right answer is to build less.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I BRING (3-up) -->
  <section class="why-section">
    <div class="mk-wrap">
      <div class="mk-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px;"><b>//</b> What you get</div>
      <h2 class="mk-h2">Three things most shops can't offer.</h2>
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-1">
          <div class="n">01</div>
          <h3 class="mk-h3">Enterprise rigor</h3>
          <p>Auth, audit trails, secrets management, threat modeling, secure data handling. Built in from the start — not retrofitted after a pen test.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-2">
          <div class="n">02</div>
          <h3 class="mk-h3">Operational fluency</h3>
          <p>An ops background means I read your workflow before I write a line of code. The first question is rarely "what should it look like" — it's "what work is this actually doing?"</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-3">
          <div class="n">03</div>
          <h3 class="mk-h3">AI as engineering, not theater</h3>
          <p>RAG, agents, copilots, automation — embedded where they reduce real friction. Evaluated, instrumented, and guardrailed. Not a chatbot bolted onto a footer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRINCIPLE / PULL QUOTE -->
  <section style="background:var(--blue-500); border-top:2px solid var(--ink-900); border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink-900);">
    <div class="mk-wrap" style="padding:80px 32px; max-width:900px;">
      <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:rgba(255,255,255,.7); margin-bottom:20px;">// Principle</div>
      <p style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:900; font-size:42px; line-height:1.1; letter-spacing:-.02em; color:#fff; margin:0;">"If you can't explain why the software did something, you don't have a product — you have a liability."</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-band" style="background:var(--ink-900);">
    <div class="cta-band-inner">
      <h2 class="mk-h2" style="color:#fff;">Talk to the<br>person who'd build it.</h2>
      <a href="/contact/" class="mk-btn mk-btn--yellow mk-btn--lg">
        Start a Project Conversation <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
